Brioche à tête
16
Rich yeast brioche with butter and eggs, shaped as brioche à tête.
---
Brioche dough
T55 bread flour|500|g
semi-skimmed milk|150|ml
eggs|240|g
fresh yeast|20|g
fine salt|10|g
powdered sugar|40|g
soft butter|150|g
---
Make the dough: put the flour, salt, sugar, crumbled yeast, eggs and milk in the bowl.
Knead on low then medium speed for about 10 min until the dough is smooth.
Add the butter in pieces and keep kneading until the dough pulls away from the sides.
Check that the dough temperature is around 23–25°C.

Leave to proof 60 min at room temperature.
Chill the dough 30 min to relax it.

Divide into pieces of about 60 g.
Shape into balls then form brioches à tête (main ball + small ball on top).
Place in buttered brioche tins.

Proof 40 to 60 min in a warm place until well risen.
Preheat the oven to 160–180°C.
Brush with egg wash.
Bake 15 to 20 min depending on size, until golden.
---
Respect proofing, resting and final proof for a soft crumb.
The dough should be soft but hold its shape — neither too stiff nor too sticky.
Adjust oven temperature to your oven (gentle heat for a well-developed brioche).
